WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.080 --> 00:00:05.060
Earlier this year, Smile introduced the world
to a curse that seems unbeatable; a demon

00:00:05.060 --> 00:00:09.360
that passes on through trauma and can create
hallucinations that are so real, you begin

00:00:09.360 --> 00:00:12.170
to question literally everything around you.

00:00:12.170 --> 00:00:15.920
So what do you do when your senses start to
be used as weapons against you?

00:00:15.920 --> 00:00:18.320
You turn to this episode, that's what.

00:00:18.320 --> 00:00:19.800
I have a solution.

00:00:19.800 --> 00:00:23.053
Here's how you beat the unbeatable demon of
Smile.

00:00:26.621 --> 00:00:27.870
Hello Internet!

00:00:27.870 --> 00:00:33.460
Welcome to Film Theory, the show that knows
exactly how to turn that frown upside down.

00:00:33.460 --> 00:00:34.460
How?

00:00:34.460 --> 00:00:35.460
By clicking the unsubscribe button.

00:00:35.460 --> 00:00:36.460
See?

00:00:36.460 --> 00:00:37.520
Doesn't it make you feel a little bit better?

00:00:37.520 --> 00:00:39.630
Well, at the very least, it made me feel better.

00:00:39.630 --> 00:00:45.513
Today we're talking about Smile, the 2022
horror film that was an absolutely massive hit.

00:00:45.513 --> 00:00:50.090
Critics loved it, audiences loved it, and
the accountants really loved it, you know,

00:00:50.090 --> 00:00:53.859
because it made $216 million off a $17 million
budget.

00:00:53.859 --> 00:00:55.020
Not too shabby.

00:00:55.020 --> 00:00:59.730
One reason for that massive success, the curse
that drives the action forward is unbeatable.

00:00:59.730 --> 00:01:04.629
You see, the story follows Dr. Rose Cotter,
a psychiatrist who was traumatized after witnessing

00:01:04.629 --> 00:01:08.630
one of her patients slice off her face while
wearing a big old, creepy grin.

00:01:08.630 --> 00:01:12.900
That alone would be horrible enough, but things
get way worse once Rose starts seeing people

00:01:12.900 --> 00:01:15.888
with that same creepy smile all around her.

00:01:20.780 --> 00:01:25.009
Eventually she realized that she's been cursed
by this evil entity that isn't really given

00:01:25.009 --> 00:01:26.009
a name in the movies.

00:01:26.009 --> 00:01:27.710
It's not even clear what this thing's supposed
to be.

00:01:27.710 --> 00:01:28.408
Ghost?

00:01:28.408 --> 00:01:29.019
Monster?

00:01:29.019 --> 00:01:29.674
Demon?

00:01:29.674 --> 00:01:33.040
It's unclear. So I'm just going to keep it as, like, curse
slash demon for now.

00:01:33.040 --> 00:01:37.409
Regardless, the curse starts giving Rose
vivid and terrifying hallucinations, which

00:01:37.409 --> 00:01:39.790
causes her to push away from all her loved
ones.

00:01:39.790 --> 00:01:43.200
Eventually she learns that the curse is passing
along through trauma, and that the only way

00:01:43.200 --> 00:01:46.579
to get rid of it is to pass it along by causing
someone else trauma.

00:01:46.579 --> 00:01:49.800
Otherwise, you're just stuck waiting for it
to eventually claim your life.

00:01:49.800 --> 00:01:53.612
A ticking clock that the movie tells us maxes
out at around four days.

00:01:59.079 --> 00:02:02.290
It's a terrifying premise that makes for a
fantastic film.

00:02:02.290 --> 00:02:05.210
But you all know me at this point, loyal theorists,
I’m not just going to sit back and let the

00:02:05.210 --> 00:02:10.820
jump scares wash over me as I munch my popcorn
and drink out of my gallon sized jug of Diet Coke.

00:02:10.820 --> 00:02:15.470
While I was in the theater my theorist cogs
started to turn wondering what Rose or anyone

00:02:15.470 --> 00:02:17.640
infected with this thing could do to beat
it.

00:02:17.640 --> 00:02:21.170
Surely there's got to be a strategy here that
we can work out to either break the Smile

00:02:21.170 --> 00:02:25.150
demon's curse, or just play into its rules
in a way that makes everyone happy in the end.

00:02:25.150 --> 00:02:27.050
So I looked online to see if anyone had one.

00:02:27.050 --> 00:02:28.050
And no, actually.

00:02:28.050 --> 00:02:29.050
Not really.

00:02:29.050 --> 00:02:30.670
No one came up with anything.

00:02:30.670 --> 00:02:31.670
Or, let me correct myself,

00:02:31.670 --> 00:02:36.313
no one came up with anything that kept us
alive and also didn't kill a bunch of other people.

00:02:36.313 --> 00:02:40.800
So today I wanted to see if we could possibly
beat this unbeatable challenge.

00:02:40.800 --> 00:02:45.330
Is it possible to create a strategy that will
put a smile on everyone's face?

00:02:45.330 --> 00:02:47.050
And not in the creepy, cursed way.

00:02:47.050 --> 00:02:48.120
Strap in, friends.

00:02:48.120 --> 00:02:49.209
We're about to find out.

00:02:49.209 --> 00:02:52.600
Let's start with the most suggested method
and the one that we actually see Rose try

00:02:52.600 --> 00:02:54.440
in the movie: Complete Isolation.

00:02:54.440 --> 00:02:58.210
You can't pass on the demon through trauma
if there's no one to pass it on to.

00:02:58.210 --> 00:02:58.980
Right?

00:02:58.980 --> 00:03:00.000
Well, it might work in theory.

00:03:00.000 --> 00:03:03.210
In Horror Movie Theory…rwrw.

00:03:03.210 --> 00:03:04.210
Way too many syllables.

00:03:04.210 --> 00:03:05.210
But in practice.

00:03:05.210 --> 00:03:07.299
No, no, no, not so much.

00:03:07.299 --> 00:03:10.700
Isolating yourself completely is something
that's way easier said than done.

00:03:10.700 --> 00:03:14.873
In the movie we watch as Rose tries to isolate
herself in her mother's abandoned house.

00:03:19.850 --> 00:03:23.550
While there she confronts the childhood trauma
that's haunted her throughout her entire life.

00:03:23.550 --> 00:03:26.330
She processes it and she basically defeats
the demon.

00:03:26.330 --> 00:03:28.142
Isolation for the win, am I right?

00:03:28.142 --> 00:03:29.142
Wrong.

00:03:29.142 --> 00:03:34.040
What at first seemed like a victory for Rose
was actually just an incredibly elaborate hallucination.

00:03:34.040 --> 00:03:36.200
Rose never beat the Smile demon.

00:03:36.200 --> 00:03:40.349
In fact, she lured the demon's next victim
to this isolated area, and then passed it

00:03:40.349 --> 00:03:41.510
along to him.

00:03:41.510 --> 00:03:45.540
But okay, what if Rose were stronger or she
was able to see through the hallucinations?

00:03:45.540 --> 00:03:46.970
Could it have worked in that case?

00:03:46.970 --> 00:03:48.060
Well, no again.

00:03:48.060 --> 00:03:51.030
Assuming you're not a billionaire, you're
going to need to go to work to pay for stuff.

00:03:51.030 --> 00:03:54.950
And while you could work from home, you got
to have something to eat, which means getting

00:03:54.950 --> 00:03:57.530
everything delivered to your door, a.k.a.

00:03:57.530 --> 00:03:58.530
delivery people.

00:03:58.530 --> 00:04:00.450
Or it means going to the grocery store, a.k.a.

00:04:00.450 --> 00:04:03.069
being surrounded by some of the most aggressive
people on the planet.

00:04:03.069 --> 00:04:07.689
Okay, so I suppose you could do it if you
were able to avoid the hallucinations and

00:04:07.689 --> 00:04:11.510
you worked from home and had everything delivered
by a remote drone.

00:04:11.510 --> 00:04:16.400
But even then, even if those huge conditions
were all in place, there's still a massive

00:04:16.400 --> 00:04:17.900
problem with this solution.

00:04:17.900 --> 00:04:19.570
This plan has to be permanent.

00:04:19.570 --> 00:04:22.150
There would be no breaks to your isolation.

00:04:22.150 --> 00:04:25.870
Every day for the rest of your life would
be spent alone without anyone or anything

00:04:25.870 --> 00:04:28.480
to talk to other than the demon tormenting
you.

00:04:28.480 --> 00:04:32.090
And even without the supernatural element
here, social isolation to this degree would

00:04:32.090 --> 00:04:34.060
be really bad for your brain.

00:04:34.060 --> 00:04:37.520
Studies have shown that socially isolated
people are more likely to suffer cognitive

00:04:37.520 --> 00:04:38.860
decline, memory loss, dementia.

00:04:38.860 --> 00:04:41.850
Impaired concentration, depression, anxiety.

00:04:41.850 --> 00:04:46.600
All in all, the isolation strategy requires
an insane number of difficult qualifiers to

00:04:46.600 --> 00:04:51.280
work perfectly and would still ultimately
lead you to a hard life full of mental anguish

00:04:51.280 --> 00:04:52.620
forever alone.

00:04:52.620 --> 00:04:56.530
In the end, I wouldn't necessarily classify
that as beating the Smile curse.

00:04:56.530 --> 00:04:58.020
So let's keep looking, shall we?

00:04:58.020 --> 00:05:01.340
One other solution I saw proposed by the channel
Wolfman's Got Nards.

00:05:01.340 --> 00:05:05.350
Incredible channel name, by the way, was based
on the idea of controlling who you pass your

00:05:05.350 --> 00:05:06.350
trauma onto.

00:05:06.350 --> 00:05:09.780
Remember, there's more than one way to pass
on the Smile demon to the next victim.

00:05:09.780 --> 00:05:14.530
If you brutally kill someone in front of another
person, the trauma of seeing that passes the

00:05:14.530 --> 00:05:15.900
curse on to the witness.

00:05:15.900 --> 00:05:20.180
This is what the character Robert Talley did
in the movie to escape the Smile demon himself.

00:05:33.000 --> 00:05:33.659
And it worked.

00:05:33.659 --> 00:05:35.780
The demon passed on and never came back.

00:05:35.780 --> 00:05:38.810
There's just one teeny, tiny, itsy bitsy problem
with that.

00:05:38.810 --> 00:05:40.370
Robert Talley is now in prison.

00:05:40.370 --> 00:05:42.080
Also, he killed someone.

00:05:42.080 --> 00:05:43.250
That's not a great look.

00:05:43.250 --> 00:05:45.490
But, you know, for now, we're just going to
focus on the prison part.

00:05:45.490 --> 00:05:50.280
What the Wolfman’s Nards suggested was exploiting
this loophole in a systematic way; taking

00:05:50.280 --> 00:05:55.130
you, your curse and two of your closest, most
expendable friends to a remote location.

00:05:55.130 --> 00:05:58.410
Step one: Brutally off the first of your two
travel mates.

00:05:58.410 --> 00:06:01.530
That should pass the curse on to your second
friend, who's probably like, “Woah, this

00:06:01.530 --> 00:06:03.630
was not the dessert party that I was expecting.”

00:06:03.630 --> 00:06:06.390
Which leads us to step number two: Bump that
one off as well.

00:06:06.390 --> 00:06:10.030
The curse dies with him and so does the only
witness to your crime.

00:06:10.030 --> 00:06:14.040
I got to say, not only does the Wolfman have
Nards, he's also got himself a pretty solid

00:06:14.040 --> 00:06:15.040
solution here.

00:06:15.040 --> 00:06:17.910
Assuming you're thorough in cleaning up and
leaving no trace of your crime, you should

00:06:17.910 --> 00:06:18.910
be in the clear.

00:06:18.910 --> 00:06:21.160
And the demon is defeated once and for all.

00:06:21.160 --> 00:06:22.160
You survived.

00:06:22.160 --> 00:06:25.009
You don't have to live a life in isolation
and you're not in prison.

00:06:25.009 --> 00:06:26.639
Technically, you've completed the assignment.

00:06:26.639 --> 00:06:31.360
There's just, you know, two little problems
there: The dead bodies that you left in your wake.

00:06:31.360 --> 00:06:34.240
Sure, you found a solution, but was it the
best solution?

00:06:34.240 --> 00:06:36.980
It's kind of like beating a video game without
getting all the achievements.

00:06:36.980 --> 00:06:38.600
Is there a true ending here?

00:06:38.600 --> 00:06:40.930
Is there a way to do a pacifist run?

00:06:40.930 --> 00:06:43.860
Survive, stay out of prison and kill zero
people?

00:06:43.860 --> 00:06:45.800
We gotta at least try, right?

00:06:45.800 --> 00:06:48.070
Okay, so what else do we know about this curse?

00:06:48.070 --> 00:06:52.139
Well, the Smile demon doesn't seem to be able
to manifest itself in any physical way.

00:06:52.139 --> 00:06:55.260
Any time we see it manipulate something in
the real world, it's quickly revealed to be

00:06:55.260 --> 00:06:58.340
a hallucination happening inside the mind
of the current victim.

00:06:58.340 --> 00:07:02.000
For example, here: while taking the form of
Rose's sister, Holly, it knocks on the car

00:07:02.000 --> 00:07:03.620
window, but it isn't actually there.

00:07:03.620 --> 00:07:07.530
Or here when it makes Rose believe that she's
gotten a call from her home security company.

00:07:07.530 --> 00:07:10.750
But the phone disappears from her hand when
a real call comes through.

00:07:10.750 --> 00:07:14.080
At first, the solution here seems like it
should be to set up totems, kind of like in

00:07:14.080 --> 00:07:17.280
Inception; things that can help you realize
what is and isn't real.

00:07:17.280 --> 00:07:21.180
In that movie, the main character used a spinning
top to determine if he was in a dream or not.

00:07:21.180 --> 00:07:23.770
So could we potentially set up something like
this to help with Rose?

00:07:23.770 --> 00:07:25.240
Well, no, probably not.

00:07:25.240 --> 00:07:29.190
Like I just said, we see that the Smile demon’s
able to completely hijack someone's senses

00:07:29.190 --> 00:07:31.660
to create incredibly realistic fantasies.

00:07:31.660 --> 00:07:35.250
It's even able to completely change Rose's
perception of the gift that she's preparing

00:07:35.250 --> 00:07:36.250
for her nephew.

00:07:36.250 --> 00:07:38.250
Though she thinks she's wrapping up a toy
train.

00:07:38.250 --> 00:07:39.770
It's actually a dead cat.

00:07:39.770 --> 00:07:43.379
If the Smile demon is able to make her think
her bloody and furry cat is a toy train, I

00:07:43.379 --> 00:07:47.400
kinda doubt that there would be any way to
find an item, sound or visual cue that would

00:07:47.400 --> 00:07:49.470
ground Rose back to reality.

00:07:49.470 --> 00:07:51.970
Rose's senses are always going to betray her.

00:07:51.970 --> 00:07:54.479
The hallucinations are just too strong.

00:07:54.479 --> 00:07:57.900
So what if we could just remove the hallucinations?

00:07:57.900 --> 00:08:02.050
That then would largely remove the curse as
power, as its only mode of attack is by mentally

00:08:02.050 --> 00:08:03.050
breaking you down.

00:08:03.050 --> 00:08:05.340
Like I said before, it doesn't have physical
power.

00:08:05.340 --> 00:08:07.190
It only has mental power.

00:08:07.190 --> 00:08:08.699
There's just one problem.

00:08:08.699 --> 00:08:12.310
Hallucinations are incredibly complex and
still poorly understood by science.

00:08:12.310 --> 00:08:15.819
The current working theory is that they're
based on the brain failing to properly select

00:08:15.819 --> 00:08:18.379
which stimuli to focus on and which to ignore.

00:08:18.379 --> 00:08:21.550
For instance, an auditory hallucination, which
are the most common types.

00:08:21.550 --> 00:08:25.240
They might be caused by the brain doing a
bit of self-talk, but then accidentally thinking

00:08:25.240 --> 00:08:26.930
that those words were said aloud.

00:08:26.930 --> 00:08:31.590
And what makes hallucinations especially tricky
is that they're spread out across the brain.

00:08:31.590 --> 00:08:34.960
Because they're actively tricking your senses,
they activate all over the brain depending

00:08:34.960 --> 00:08:37.361
on what type of hallucination you're talking
about.

00:08:37.361 --> 00:08:41.680
Auditory hallucinations are associated with
activation of the middle and superior temporal

00:08:41.680 --> 00:08:44.459
cortex; areas involved in processing speech.

00:08:44.459 --> 00:08:48.180
Somatic hallucinations, basically phantom
sensations inside your body.

00:08:48.180 --> 00:08:51.290
Those are associated with the parts of the
brain that are usually processing the sense

00:08:51.290 --> 00:08:52.290
of touch.

00:08:52.290 --> 00:08:55.500
So really, to fight the curse’s hold over
your brain, you're going to have to fight

00:08:55.500 --> 00:08:59.829
on the battleground of your brain and you're
going to be fighting multiple fronts all at

00:08:59.829 --> 00:09:00.880
the same time.

00:09:00.880 --> 00:09:04.800
Making things even more complicated are the
neurotransmitters involved.

00:09:04.800 --> 00:09:08.420
At this point I'm sure you know that neurotransmitters
are the chemical messengers in the brain that

00:09:08.420 --> 00:09:10.870
allow nerve impulses to travel between cells.

00:09:10.870 --> 00:09:11.870
Right?

00:09:11.870 --> 00:09:13.950
The one you always hear about is dopamine,
that's the reward chemical.

00:09:13.950 --> 00:09:17.460
You do something good or rewarding and your
brain suddenly gets flooded with dopamine

00:09:17.460 --> 00:09:21.439
as a big old pat on the back, or pat on the
cerebellum.

00:09:21.439 --> 00:09:24.670
Hallucinations in your brain, though they're
not as simple as that 1 to 1 relationship,

00:09:24.670 --> 00:09:28.220
researchers believe that they involve no less
than five separate neurotransmitters.

00:09:28.220 --> 00:09:30.920
And it's not like the levels are too high
or too low.

00:09:30.920 --> 00:09:33.980
They require levels to neither be too high
nor too low.

00:09:33.980 --> 00:09:35.420
Striking a tricky balance.

00:09:35.420 --> 00:09:39.470
So knowing all of this, is there a way to
fight off the hallucinations in a healthy,

00:09:39.470 --> 00:09:40.516
responsible way?

00:09:40.516 --> 00:09:41.444
Yes.

00:09:41.444 --> 00:09:45.550
If you look at Rose's symptoms after she gets
infected by the curse, her condition is shockingly

00:09:45.550 --> 00:09:50.230
similar to the psychotic disorder of schizophrenia,
which is characterized first and foremost

00:09:50.230 --> 00:09:51.610
by hallucinations.

00:09:51.610 --> 00:09:56.820
In fact, according to the Diagnostic and Statistical
Manual of Mental Disorders, or DSM, for short:

00:09:56.820 --> 00:10:01.220
persistent supernatural hallucinations, coupled
with a significant disturbance in work performance

00:10:01.220 --> 00:10:05.580
and interpersonal functioning, are some of
the top criteria for diagnosing someone with

00:10:05.580 --> 00:10:11.590
schizophrenia and Rose in the movie is basically
speed running her way to that very diagnosis.

00:10:11.590 --> 00:10:15.560
Fortunately, this means that help may be out
there to treat the symptoms that she's experiencing.

00:10:15.560 --> 00:10:20.140
Antipsychotic medications like Clozapine are
specifically prescribed to relieve hallucinations

00:10:20.140 --> 00:10:21.830
for people suffering from schizophrenia.

00:10:21.830 --> 00:10:26.170
They can help calm down and clear confusion
in a person with acute psychosis within a

00:10:26.170 --> 00:10:31.160
matter of days or even hours, exactly the
sort of treatment time that we need for a

00:10:31.160 --> 00:10:33.720
fast acting hallucination based curse.

00:10:33.720 --> 00:10:35.510
Now, that is a huge win.

00:10:35.510 --> 00:10:39.410
We're getting the treatment we need to silence
the mechanisms that the curse is using to

00:10:39.410 --> 00:10:40.410
attack us.

00:10:40.410 --> 00:10:42.410
But pharmacological solutions aren't going
to be enough here.

00:10:42.410 --> 00:10:45.079
Whether you're talking about schizophrenia
or the smile curse.

00:10:45.079 --> 00:10:49.149
You see, individuals suffering from extreme
hallucinations tend to be less likely to take

00:10:49.149 --> 00:10:50.149
their medication.

00:10:50.149 --> 00:10:51.680
This happens for multiple reasons.

00:10:51.680 --> 00:10:52.930
They may deny their illness.

00:10:52.930 --> 00:10:54.980
They may have paranoia about the medication.

00:10:54.980 --> 00:10:56.399
They might not think they need it anymore.

00:10:56.399 --> 00:11:00.459
And the numbers here are telling, depending
on the report you read, anywhere between 37%

00:11:00.459 --> 00:11:06.380
and 74% of patients will stop their medication
prematurely, and that is going to greatly

00:11:06.380 --> 00:11:08.020
increase the risk of relapse.

00:11:08.020 --> 00:11:12.780
So to avoid the risk, Rose would also need
to be receiving some form of psychotherapy.

00:11:12.780 --> 00:11:16.740
The incidence of schizophrenia relapse among
patients receiving therapy compared to those

00:11:16.740 --> 00:11:20.589
without is roughly 18% versus 60%.

00:11:20.589 --> 00:11:22.350
That is a massive difference.

00:11:22.350 --> 00:11:25.250
Now, to be fair, this isn't a full out solution.

00:11:25.250 --> 00:11:27.830
The demon won't be destroyed in her brain
or anything.

00:11:27.830 --> 00:11:29.120
It'll just be silenced.

00:11:29.120 --> 00:11:31.279
It won't have a means of attacking anymore.

00:11:31.279 --> 00:11:35.660
It's a thing that will need to be maintained,
lived with, rather than defeated, which honestly

00:11:35.660 --> 00:11:37.779
is pretty darn fitting for the movie.

00:11:37.779 --> 00:11:41.510
Sure, on paper Smile’s about a demonic curse that
passes from person to person.

00:11:41.510 --> 00:11:42.179
Fine.

00:11:42.179 --> 00:11:45.620
But what it's really about is mental health
and cycles of trauma.

00:11:45.620 --> 00:11:50.589
I mean, the literal premise is putting on
a fake smile when just under the surface you're

00:11:50.589 --> 00:11:51.589
in mental anguish.

00:11:51.589 --> 00:11:53.769
It doesn't get much more clear cut than that.

00:11:53.769 --> 00:11:57.579
All of the other solutions that I talked about
today; isolating yourself, trying to hurt

00:11:57.579 --> 00:12:00.960
others, they're all unhealthy ways of dealing
with mental illness.

00:12:00.960 --> 00:12:05.209
But asking for help, taking medication, learning
to live with mental illness and trauma.

00:12:05.209 --> 00:12:09.649
They're the obvious answers that so many people
sadly avoid because of how much stigma comes

00:12:09.649 --> 00:12:11.470
attached to mental health issues.

00:12:11.470 --> 00:12:16.279
And while Smile ends on a negative note, these
real world situations don't have to.

00:12:16.279 --> 00:12:19.769
Rose refused to acknowledge what was happening
to her until it was much too late, and when

00:12:19.769 --> 00:12:22.870
she did turn to others to help, no one around
her believed her.

00:12:22.870 --> 00:12:24.500
Let that be the lesson today.

00:12:24.500 --> 00:12:29.190
Be open and willing to listen with an open
mind when someone cries out for help and don't

00:12:29.190 --> 00:12:31.459
always trust the smile on the outside.

00:12:31.459 --> 00:12:33.420
We can be seriously hurting inside.

00:12:33.420 --> 00:12:37.930
By helping each other, then and only then
can we truly defeat the demon.

00:12:37.930 --> 00:12:40.343
But hey, that's just a theory.

00:12:40.343 --> 00:12:42.604
A FILM THEORY!

00:12:42.604 --> 00:12:44.114
aaaaaaaaaaaaand cut.

